{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794353484,"nonce":"PtOIlzNqpA+WcrwQiVnF4dY+ymY=","title":"exponential() defaults to a lumped mass: a different system from every other scheme","message":"The default mass='lumped' integrates the row-sum lumped semidiscrete system. Against the consistent system all other schemes solve, it is 4e-2 off on P1 triangles, 8e-2 on Q1 hexes, 5e-3 on P3, while mass='consistent' is 1e-8. Lumping is now refused where row sums are not positive (P2, Hermite, N1E). Open question whether the default should be consistent.","files":null}]}